node_modules/

# Next.js build output
.next/
out/

# Auto-regenerated by `next dev`/`next build` on every run (points at either
# .next/dev/types/routes.d.ts or .next/types/routes.d.ts depending on which
# was last run locally) — never meaningful to commit, and committing the dev
# variant breaks nothing at runtime (Next rewrites it before every build) but
# is confusing repo noise. See docs root-cause notes for the PR #122 incident.
next-env.d.ts

